    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-3" id="fn-3" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">On page 200, line 22, column (c), the Total In Service Depreciation figure of $1,235,358,284 includes $1,365,191 of accumulated depreciation related to operating lease right-of-use assets. If the accumulated depreciation related to right-of-use assets was excluded it would result in a figure of $1,233,993,093.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The company has power contracts with each Yankees Company that require the company to pay an amount equal to its share of total fixed and operating costs of the plant plus a return on equity.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Regulatory flow through other tax asset - AFUDC</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The following are FERC related CTC Dockets:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">FERC Docket No. ER97-678-000 and ER98-6-000.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">MA DPU Docket No. D.T.E. 96-25 and 97-94.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Pension/Other Post-retirement Employee Benefits.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Deficient accumulated deferred income taxes resulting from the remeasurement of the company&#8217;s deferred tax balances due to a change in Massachusetts income tax rate.</span>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"></span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Under ASC 410-20 the Company is required to for certain legal obligations associated with the retirement of long-live assets must be recognized at their fair value, at the time the obligations are incurred, where as upon the initial recognition of a legal liability, these costs must be capitalized as part of the long-live asset and depreciated over the life of the asset. Also the company must recorded the depreciation related to the cost of removal of the asset upon retirement. As a result, the Company records the legal obligation treated to future asset retirement activities related to certain tangible capital assets, which are recognized as a liability. The Company has a legal obligation to perform the asset retirement activity, however the timing and/or method of settlement are conditional, and dependent on future events, that are not within the control of the company, however the obligation to perform the retirement activity is unconditional. Accordingly, an entity is required to recognize a liability for the fair value of a conditional asset retirement obligation if the fair value of the liability can be reasonably estimated. The fair value of a liability for the conditional asset retirement obligation should be recognized when incurred&#8212;generally upon acquisition, construction, or development and (or) through the normal operation of the asset. The company recovers in rates the retirement obligations incurred by the Company.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Deficient accumulated deferred income taxes resulting from the remeasurement of the company&#8217;s deferred tax balances due to a change in state apportionment resulting from the sale of its Rhode Island business.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">The CTC resulted from a FERC-approved wholesale settlement that restructured the whole contractual relationship between New England Power Company ("NEP" and MECo in the context of the restructuring the electric utility industry in Massachusetts. NEP terminated its all-requirements contractual agreement with MECO in exchange for the payment of CTC by MECO.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">New England Power Company, FERC Docket Nos.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">ER97-678-000 (1997) and ER98-6-000 (1998); New England Company.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">D.T.E.97, at 11 (1998)</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">The CTC resulted from a FERC-approved wholesale settlement that restructured the whole contractual relationship between New England Power Company ("NEP" and MECo in the context of the restructuring the electric utility industry in Massachusetts. NEP terminated its all-requirements contractual agreement with MECO in exchange for the payment of CTC by MECo.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">New England Power Company, FERC Docket Nos.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">ER97-678-000 (1997) and ER98-6-000 (1998); New England Company.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">D.T.E.97, at 11 (1998)</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">Excess accumulated deferred income taxes resulting from the remeasurement of the company's deferred tax balances due to the enactment of the 2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">Excess accumulated deferred income taxes resulting from the remeasurement of the company's deferred tax balances due to the enactment of the 2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">Offset Allowance for Funds Used During Construction - New England East West Solution Project - FERC Docket No. ER08-1548-0000. The accrued AFUDC balance as of November 2011 is to be amortized over 45 year depreciable life of the NEEWS assets thru November 2056.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">On June 29, 2018 the Participating Transmission Owners Administrative Committee (which includes New England Power Company), reached an initial settlement agreement with the FERC and other interested parties related to Docket Nos. EL-16-19-000 and ER20-2054. This initial settlement was rejected by FERC in May 2019. Settlement discussions resumed and a revised uncontested settlement (&#8220;Settlement Agreement&#8221;) was filed in June 2020 and approved by FERC on December 28, 2020. In the Settlement Agreement, the settling parties agreed to adopt certain changes to the ISO-NE Open Access Transmission Tariff (&#8220;OATT&#8221;), including replacing the existing regional and local formula rates under the OATT with a new formula rate based on spreadsheets (or templates), adopting transparency related formula rate protocols and introducing several other new Appendices that all will be found under the umbrella of Attachment F. The Settlement agreement also details how the existing tariff and billing structures will transition to the new methodology under the Settlement Agreement. The rate agreed to in the Settlement Agreement is referred to as the &#8220;Settled Formula Rate.&#8221;</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Under the terms of the Settlement Agreement, NEP is permitted to include 50% CWIP in rate base for all transmission projects under construction on or after January 1, 2022 in the Local Service component of the Settled Formula Rate. The recovery of the return and income taxes on CWIP in rate base will be included in the Local Service component of the Settled Formula Rate.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The Settlement Agreement further provides, that, as part of the first informational filing under the Settled Formula Rate, National Grid shall include accounting procedures that comply with the Commission&#8217;s requirements documenting how Local Service customers will not be charged for capitalized AFUDC for projects that are included in CWIP in rate base as permitted by the Settlement Agreement.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">On June 29, 2018 the Participating Transmission Owners Administrative Committee (which includes New England Power Company), reached an initial settlement agreement with the FERC and other interested parties</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">related to Docket Nos. EL-16-19-000 and ER20-2054. This initial settlement was rejected by FERC in May 2019. Settlement discussions resumed and a revised uncontested settlement (&#8220;Settlement Agreement&#8221;) was filed in June 2020 and approved by FERC on December 28, 2020. In the Settlement Agreement, the settling parties agreed to adopt certain changes to the ISO-NE Open Access Transmission Tariff (&#8220;OATT&#8221;), including replacing the existing regional and local formula rates under the OATT with a new formula rate based on spreadsheets (or templates), adopting transparency related formula rate protocols and introducing several other new Appendices that all will be found under the umbrella of Attachment F. The Settlement agreement also details how the existing tariff and billing structures will transition to the new methodology under the Settlement Agreement. The rate agreed to in the Settlement Agreement is referred to as the &#8220;Settled Formula Rate.&#8221;</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Under the terms of the Settlement Agreement, NEP is permitted to include 50% CWIP in rate base for all transmission projects under construction on or after January 1, 2022 in the Local Service component of the Settled Formula Rate. The recovery of the return and income taxes on CWIP in rate base will be included in the Local Service component of the Settled Formula Rate.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The Settlement Agreement further provides, that, as part of the first informational filing under the Settled Formula Rate, National Grid shall include accounting procedures that comply with the Commission&#8217;s requirements documenting how Local Service customers will not be charged for capitalized AFUDC for projects that are included in CWIP in rate base as permitted by the Settlement Agreement.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">Regulatory flow through - other</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">Represents the Company&#8217;s unamortized non-cash accrual of net pension and postretirement benefit other than pension (PBOP) actuarial gains and losses, which is partially offset by the excess amounts received in rates over actual costs of the Company&#8217;s PBOP expense.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">On July 31, 2023, NEP filed a revised fixed expense amount for transmission related Post Retirement Benefit Worksheet 9 that describes Company&#8217;s Transmission PBOP expense for CY 2022, as part of NEP&#8217;s Annual Transmission Revenue Requirement filing. In CY22, NEP&#8217;s actual PBOP expense was a net credit of $2.2 million but NEP is allowed to recover a fixed amount of $167K therefore an over-recovery of $2.5 million, inclusive of interest for CY22. NEP will refund the over recovery to customers in CY25. In CY23, NEP&#8217;s additional PBOP over-recovery is $3 million, inclusive of interest. In CY24, NEP's additional PBOP over-recovery is $0.7m.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">'On October 17, 2023, ISO New England Inc. (ISO-NE) filed, on behalf of NEP, a revised Appendix A to Attachment F of the ISO-NE Open Access Transmission Tariff to update NEP's fixed expense amount for transmission related post-retirement benefits other than pensions ("PBOPs"). On December 5, 2023, the Commission issued a delegated letter order accepting the filing effective January 1, 2024.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:92%">Regulatory liability established under the FERC-approved 2020 ISO-NE transmission formula rate settlement, representing the difference between amounts authorized for recovery under the Settled Formula Rate and amounts billed to customers.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
